WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.427 --> 00:00:04.538
Unit fifteen. Digital Research Citations!

2
00:00:05.474 --> 00:00:10.450
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.967
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:15.017 --> 00:00:19.509
Today we learn about Digital Research Citations. Let's go!

5
00:00:20.214 --> 00:00:24.544
Citation. Say it with me. Citation!

6
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:32.038
Source. Say it with me. Source!

7
00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:39.182
Credit. Say it with me. Credit!

8
00:00:42.636 --> 00:00:46.836
Plagiarism. Say it with me. Plagiarism!

9
00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:55.133
Bibliography. Say it with me. Bibliography!

10
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.583
Reference. Say it with me. Reference!

11
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.794
Author. Say it with me. Author!

12
00:01:13.313 --> 00:01:17.521
Give credit. Say it with me. Give credit!

13
00:01:21.021 --> 00:01:29.546
A digital research citation gives credit to a source and author. Proper citation in a bibliography helps avoid plagiarism.

14
00:01:29.596 --> 00:01:32.840
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:39.280
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.480
Credit!

17
00:01:41.454 --> 00:01:46.967
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:48.167
Author!

19
00:01:49.101 --> 00:01:57.753
Did you know? There are different citation styles, like APA and MLA, each with its own specific rules for giving credit!

20
00:01:57.803 --> 00:02:00.221
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:11.769
Think and answer. Why is it important to give credit to a source when you use their information?

22
00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:12.969
Great answer!

23
00:02:13.918 --> 00:02:19.300
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:22.559
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

